  "surprises": [
    "A federal means-tested benefit where the prominent number (MAPR) is neither an income ceiling nor a benefit cap -- it is a target the payment fills to. 'Income below MAPR' is a common wrong shorthand; the real test is countable income (net of medical-expense deductions) plus a net-worth limit."
